A '''tram''' was a passenger vehicle employing [[repulsorlift]] technology for hover-based movement. Unlike typical repulsorlift vehicles, it featured a unique guidance rod system, embedded in a road-based track.<ref name="SC 101" /> Trams were typically operated by [[RX-series pilot droid]]s.<ref name="SC 101 EG" />

Trams were designed with a single, unpartitioned car with an accordion joint, accommodating flexibility in motion. Their interior contained double seats arranged around a gangway, with a bench seat at the rear. In addition, they were equipped with large panoramic [[viewport]]s and automatic sliding doors for ease of access. Passengers were generally required to remain seated when the tram was in motion.<ref name="SC 101" />

In the [[New Republic Era]], trams were utilized on the [[planet]] [[At Attin]],<ref name="SC 101" /> an isolated [[Jewels of the Old Republic|Jewel of the Old Republic]].<ref name="SC 103">{{SkeletonCrew|Very Interesting, As an Astrogation Problem}}</ref> In addition, At Attin residents could use [[school tram]]s, which connected [[Unidentified city (At Attin)|a city]] with its suburbs, sharing traffic roads with other vehicles or using dedicated underpasses to deliver students to [[At Attin Middle School Gamma]]. Young tram commuters were notorious for disobeying the [[pilot]]'s commands, with some unruly minors sticking [[gum]] to the back of<ref name="SC 101" /> his<ref name="SC 101 AD">{{SkeletonCrew|This Could Be a Real Adventure}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> head.<ref name="SC 101" /> Before departure, [[youngling]]s would wait for their school trams at designated locations and at specific [[time]]s. Running late for a tram could mean having to cover the tram's distance on one's own, an incident that happened to the [[human]]<ref name="SC 101" /> schoolboy<ref name="Wim">{{Databank|wim|Wim}}</ref> [[Wim]], who<ref name="SC 101" /> around [[9 ABY]]<ref name="SCDate">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> attempted to get to school by [[hoverbike]] instead, using a non-standard detour through the [[Forest|woods]].<ref name="SC 101" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|We didn't want to go so obvious as to turn it yellow. But there are very similar form languages in there and that was very specific because we didn't want to turn it into a subway car. It's a school bus, but our Star Wars version.|Doug Chiang|<ref name="Baver">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-production-design-interview|text=Welcome to the Worlds of ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'': An Interview with Doug Chiang and Oliver Scholl|author=[[Kristin Baver]]|date=2024-12-14}}</ref>}}
Trams first appeared in the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'', making their in-universe debut in "[[This Could Be a Real Adventure]],"<ref name="SC 101" /> the pilot episode that was aired on [[Disney+]] on [[December 2]], [[2024]].<ref name="Premiere">{{Twitter|StarWars|status/1861409832349172011|[[Star Wars]]|quote=Mark your calendars. 🗓️ On December 2, stream the two-episode series premiere of #SkeletonCrew, only on @DisneyPlus.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/QwMYe}}</ref> Before the two-episode premiere took place, trams were presented in several promotional clips and videos,<ref name="SWYouTube-Skeleton Crew &#124; Jude Law at D23 &#124; Disney+">{{SWYouTube|fP6oFCM7qfE|Skeleton Crew &#124; Jude Law at D23 &#124; Disney+}}</ref><ref name="UGCnRahQDFE">{{SWYouTube|UGCnRahQDFE|Skeleton Crew &#124; Filmmaker Roundtable &#124; Disney+}}</ref><ref name="VfjM_K_b2is">{{SWYouTube|VfjM_K_b2is|Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Clip &#124; Streaming Dec 2 on Disney+}}</ref> including the two trailers that were released on [[August 10]], 2024 and [[November 1]], 2024, respectively.<ref name="SWYouTube-Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Streaming December 3 on Disney+">{{SWYouTube|a6voXgBlmpk|Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Streaming December 3 on Disney+|date=2024-08-10}}</ref><ref name="SWYouTube-Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+">{{SWYouTube|f19gfOMZTtg|Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|date=2024-11-01}}</ref>

According to co-production designer [[Doug Chiang]], [[school tram]]s presented in ''[[Star Wars]]: Skeleton Crew'' were a "''[[Star Wars]]'' version" of [[wikipedia:United States of America|American]] [[wikipedia:School bus|school buses]]. Even so, the creators decided not to introduce yellow trams so as not to make the school-bus–reference too explicit.<ref name="Baver" /> In addition, sound editor [[David W. Collins]]—a huge fan of [[Star Tours]] and [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] theme parks—mixed a sound of one of entertainment rides, which can be heard in "This Could Be a Huge Adventure" when the school tram pulls up.<ref name="SW-The Strange and Familiar ''''Sounds of ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew''">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-skywalker-sound-interview|text=The Strange and Familiar Sounds of ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew''|author=[[Brandon Wainerdi]]|date=2024-12-26}}</ref>

